plugins/lint/ is a vendored copy, not the source.

skills/lint/ is copied verbatim from the lint repository at
the tag recorded in meta/lint.skill.yml. The copy is a whole
package, not one file: SKILL.md, the runner it invokes, and
the agent metadata each client reads. LICENSE beside this
file is that repository's licence, carried along because MIT
requires the notice to travel with a substantial copy.

    Upstream   https://github.com/trycopilotai/lint
    Copyright  (c) 2026 Try Copilot AI
    Licence    MIT

That tag is not published yet. meta/lint.skill.yml records
`upstream_sha: UNRESOLVED` rather than a commit id, because
no commit has been tagged v0.1.5 in public and writing the
one it is expected to get would make every check that exists
to catch a mismatch pass anyway. The bytes here are the
package intended for that release, and the digest recorded in
meta/ is a digest of these bytes, which is a fact about this
repository rather than a claim about the remote.

Until the tag exists, this entry is `pending-publication`:
`make release-gate` holds it, and the generated index does
not link it to an upstream that cannot be visited yet. When
v0.1.5 is pushed, `make release-gate` is what confirms the
tag resolves, the pin matches, and the published package is
byte for byte what is vendored here.

Do not edit anything under this directory. `make validate`
compares the whole vendored tree against the deterministic
digest recorded in meta/ and fails on any difference, and
`make sync` replaces the tree from upstream. Changes belong
in the upstream repository; issues and releases live there
too.
